WEBVTT

00:00:46.208 --> 00:00:48.208
You're so cute, Patty.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.000
Big Sister...

00:00:56.792 --> 00:00:58.250
Big Sister!

00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:10.750
There's still plenty more, too.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.208
Mm-hmm!

00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:32.875
Patty...

00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:57.208
<i>we wanna be there even if we had to</i>
<i>twist the world all around to get there</i>

00:01:57.208 --> 00:02:08.083
<i>without you, i guess i couldn't</i>
<i>even find the future here today</i>

00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:19.042
<i>i was always trying to take nothing for granted</i>

00:02:19.042 --> 00:02:27.083
<i>for the day i might lose them</i>

00:02:27.083 --> 00:02:34.125
<i>but you just came in to my black</i>
<i>and white monochrome destiny</i>

00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:44.292
<i>and colored it all over</i>

00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:51.667
<i>we won't be satisfied with the routine future</i>

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:59.083
<i>we were born to make a new history come true</i>

00:02:59.083 --> 00:03:06.292
<i>there's absolutely no</i>
<i>absolute thing in this world</i>

00:03:06.292 --> 00:03:10.875
<i>this road goes on forever</i>

00:03:10.875 --> 00:03:17.000
<i>as long as we won't give up</i>

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:27.125
Feh, how lame. How 'bout
we ditch class and go light up?

00:03:27.125 --> 00:03:31.500
I've gotta C-note, so let's
grab some honeys and tear it up!

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.667
Um, this is Master's shop,
so let's cut that out.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.167
Hunh? You want some of this?

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:40.750
I'll bust a cap in you! Bring it!

00:03:42.958 --> 00:03:45.583
I wish I'd never let you watch that drama.

00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:49.042
"CSI: Yo-Yo Girl Cop"

00:03:49.042 --> 00:03:51.250
The hell are you from?

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.625
I'm the hell from CSI!

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.292
Hey, you! Analyze this soil
trace that's stuck to the shoe, punk!

00:04:00.292 --> 00:04:03.083
For some reason, I'm stuck collectin' prints.

00:04:03.083 --> 00:04:06.208
Youse guys, stop screwin' around,
or you'll answer to me!

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.458
The hell are you from, punk?!

00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:12.000
Huh? I'm from DWMA, punk!

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.625
Eh? DWMA? Never heard of it.

00:04:15.625 --> 00:04:19.917
Meme, when you say it like that,
it doesn't come across as a joke.

00:04:19.917 --> 00:04:22.250
What's DWMA again?

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.375
It's the school we go to.

00:04:24.375 --> 00:04:25.792
Hey!

00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:32.500
So order something, already.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.083
I'll have a Napolitan, please.

00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:37.542
I'll take today's lunch special.

00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:39.000
P-P...

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:39.667
Hunh?

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:43.208
P-Pi... Pil... P-Pil...

00:04:46.583 --> 00:04:48.083
Whoa...

00:04:50.583 --> 00:04:52.583
Here you go.

00:04:56.917 --> 00:04:58.417
Patty...

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.625
Who could they be?

00:05:07.625 --> 00:05:10.250
They seem like the real thing.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.417
Out of sight, man.

00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:15.292
Well, no longer in our peepers, anyhow.

00:05:15.292 --> 00:05:16.833
You're still at it, I see.

00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:19.833
"This is a Real Fight!"

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.125
What a rude way to set them down!

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:29.125
Also, what I ordered was a Napolitan!

00:05:29.125 --> 00:05:31.667
Hunh? Napolitan?

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.458
Never heard of it.

00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:39.083
Well, all of Master's dishes
are delicious, so I guess it's okay.

00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:44.250
Just shut up and eat what's put
in front of you, or you'll regret it.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.458
Okay, we'll be leaving now.

00:05:46.458 --> 00:05:48.958
Yeah... good work.

00:05:55.292 --> 00:05:56.542
Master!

00:05:56.542 --> 00:05:58.250
Oh, yes?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:03.250
Those two are the Thompson sisters.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.708
They are on probation, so I wonder
if you might go easy on them.

00:06:06.708 --> 00:06:08.333
On probation?

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:13.750
As it happens, they can both
turn into weapons, like Tsugumi can.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:19.833
When they were little, they were
abandoned, in Brooklyn, New York.

00:06:19.833 --> 00:06:24.292
They had to dirty their hands in
a variety of misdeeds to get by.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:29.917
And despite having no other
choice to survive, a crime is a crime.

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:37.750
But then they were caught
by a certain VIP from DWMA.

00:06:42.208 --> 00:06:46.125
Did you notice what
they had around their wrists?

00:06:47.375 --> 00:06:50.042
Those have GPS trackers in them,

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:54.083
and they're used to allow
DWMA to know wherever they go.

00:06:54.083 --> 00:06:58.958
Indeed. It would be dangerous not
to keep an eye on those ladies.

00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:02.375
This is on the house.

00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:03.625
Oh, my!

00:07:03.625 --> 00:07:05.083
Sorry about today.

00:07:05.083 --> 00:07:07.000
Master, even among all your dishes,

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.625
your Napolitan is in a class all its own.

00:07:09.625 --> 00:07:12.083
Miss Anya, are you going to eat it <i>all</i>?

00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:14.083
<i>No </i>I'm <i>not</i>.

00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:16.625
You said they were abandoned as children,

00:07:16.625 --> 00:07:18.000
but why was that?

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.542
I haven't asked them about that.

00:07:20.542 --> 00:07:24.667
Maybe it was the fault of their weapon power.

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:26.917
It's because of their weapon power

00:07:26.917 --> 00:07:30.917
that the two of them were
able to fight this far on their own.

00:07:30.917 --> 00:07:34.917
If they didn't have their ability,
with their good looks,

00:07:34.917 --> 00:07:37.542
there's no telling where they'd be now.

00:07:38.542 --> 00:07:42.417
Hmm, the fault of being
weapons...? Because of it...?

00:07:43.917 --> 00:07:45.292
Miss Tsugumi!

00:07:45.292 --> 00:07:47.375
We're going to finish it off!

00:07:47.375 --> 00:07:49.792
Huh? No, you can't!

00:07:51.333 --> 00:07:54.042
Hold on, Miss Meme! Aren't you being a pig?

00:07:54.042 --> 00:07:55.125
Yes, I am.

00:07:55.125 --> 00:07:57.958
My! Miss Meme, you're shameless!

00:07:59.458 --> 00:08:02.208
--Miss Anya, go "Aaah..."
--"Aaah."

00:08:02.208 --> 00:08:05.458
H-Hold on! Miss Meme!

00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:09.917
That was delicious!

00:08:09.917 --> 00:08:11.542
Thank you very much.

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:17.250
Miss Meme, you've put on
a little weight, haven't you?

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:20.292
I've already forgotten what I weighed yesterday.

00:08:29.042 --> 00:08:33.083
Huh? You're those customers
from earlier, aren't you?

00:08:33.083 --> 00:08:36.292
Come to think of it, we never got our tip, huh?

00:08:36.292 --> 00:08:40.042
You don't have to leave tips at Master's shop.

00:08:40.042 --> 00:08:43.250
You work there, and you don't even know <i>that</i>?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.250
Hunh?

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:47.417
Don't go acting so tough
when you're dolled up so pretty,

00:08:47.417 --> 00:08:49.750
you spoiled little privileged girl.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.542
Let's take this around the corner.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.292
You guys are DWMA students, right?

00:08:58.292 --> 00:09:00.625
Why don't you show us how strong you are?

00:09:00.625 --> 00:09:04.625
Oh, no, while we may be at
DWMA, we're in the NOT class,

00:09:04.625 --> 00:09:06.292
so fighting is out of the question.

00:09:06.292 --> 00:09:09.167
So you're the good-for-nothing
kind of DWMA students.

00:09:10.792 --> 00:09:13.292
I don't care if we are in NOT,
after pushing us this far,

00:09:13.292 --> 00:09:14.958
we won't just stand by!

00:09:14.958 --> 00:09:15.708
But...

00:09:15.708 --> 00:09:18.708
We are still students of DWMA!

00:09:18.708 --> 00:09:21.250
Sounds to me like they wanna go at it, Patty.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:22.750
This oughta be good.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:25.333
Miss Tsugumi, transform yourself!

00:09:25.333 --> 00:09:27.042
You rube!

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:29.375
Just don't hurt them.

00:09:29.375 --> 00:09:31.875
Oh? You're going to fight?

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:48.042
What is this?

00:09:48.042 --> 00:09:50.583
Your blade hasn't even come in yet.

00:09:52.875 --> 00:09:54.000
Patty...

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.042
Okay, Big Sister.

00:09:57.875 --> 00:10:00.042
Since they're delinquents,
the weapon they turn into

00:10:00.042 --> 00:10:02.083
is probably a bat or a chain, right?

00:10:02.083 --> 00:10:04.250
Or maybe brass knuckles?

00:10:07.708 --> 00:10:09.083
A pistol?!

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:16.875
Well, what's the matter?

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:25.792
What's wrong? Too scared to take a single step?

00:10:25.792 --> 00:10:29.125
Well, I'm a close-range
weapon without even any blade,

00:10:29.125 --> 00:10:30.667
and you've got a gun...

00:10:30.667 --> 00:10:32.708
This isn't a fair fight!

00:10:32.708 --> 00:10:35.167
Hmph, of course not.

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:38.083
While the world is full
of girls blessed from birth,

00:10:38.083 --> 00:10:40.250
the opposite is true, too.

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:45.708
This is a real fight. We aren't
in any ring, and this is no sport.

00:10:45.708 --> 00:10:50.292
Anyone who bothers to fight under
equal conditions is a damned fool,

00:10:50.292 --> 00:10:53.208
or they're an obnoxious bastard,
looking down on their opponent.

00:10:53.208 --> 00:10:57.000
This might be too hard for a
babe-in-the-woods young lady like you.

00:11:01.125 --> 00:11:05.708
You wait... until after
you've beaten me to say that!

00:11:05.708 --> 00:11:10.000
Spoiled girls like you wouldn't
last three days on the street.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:14.000
Okay, come on. I'll wait for you,
and won't even shoot.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.458
Make light of me, will you?!

00:11:22.083 --> 00:11:23.833
Patty!

00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:26.500
That's right! They're weapon sisters!

00:11:30.458 --> 00:11:35.542
Like she said, right? We don't
fight under the same conditions as you.

00:11:42.125 --> 00:11:43.125
Miss Anya!

00:11:43.125 --> 00:11:44.500
Are you okay?!

00:11:45.833 --> 00:11:50.042
It's too much trouble to
cause problems while on probation,

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:52.333
so we'll let you off with just this.

00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:06.292
It is said that the first humans
that could turn into weapons

00:12:06.292 --> 00:12:09.250
were born as a result of
the research of witches.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:12.083
Using witch souls,
and their ability to transform,

00:12:12.083 --> 00:12:14.083
they joined weapons and people together,

00:12:14.083 --> 00:12:16.583
and the genes for becoming a weapon were born.

00:12:16.583 --> 00:12:20.708
Those genes became atavistic,
and that is how you came to be here.

00:12:20.708 --> 00:12:22.000
As such...

00:12:25.625 --> 00:12:27.708
We're done for today, right?

00:12:27.708 --> 00:12:29.917
Let's have lunch!

00:12:29.917 --> 00:12:32.750
Well, shall we go to Master's shop?

00:12:34.917 --> 00:12:36.667
Are you seriously asking?

00:12:36.667 --> 00:12:37.417
Uh...

00:12:37.417 --> 00:12:39.333
Don't "Uh" us!

00:12:39.333 --> 00:12:43.958
Even I will never forget that incident
that had us all but dancing with the devil!

00:12:43.958 --> 00:12:48.542
Miss Meme! I thought I asked you
to stop using that delinquent slang.

00:12:48.542 --> 00:12:50.500
Why have you not forgotten those awful words,

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.750
and instead, you've forgotten to forget?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:57.083
I forgot what? This is a little bit complicated.

00:13:00.542 --> 00:13:02.833
Ah, welcome.

00:13:02.833 --> 00:13:07.958
Oh, Meme and Miss Anya are too busy today, so...

00:13:07.958 --> 00:13:10.125
What's your problem?

00:13:10.125 --> 00:13:11.958
What an impolite waitress!

00:13:11.958 --> 00:13:15.917
Shut up. If you've got a problem,
talk to the guy that hired me.

00:13:15.917 --> 00:13:18.417
Such a pretty face for a punk, too.

00:13:18.417 --> 00:13:21.083
Huh? Stuff it, you dirty-minded coot.

00:13:23.417 --> 00:13:25.083
You...

00:13:25.083 --> 00:13:26.458
Hey!

00:13:26.458 --> 00:13:31.167
Yes! It's not like that! I certainly
didn't come to bother you!

00:13:31.167 --> 00:13:33.625
I like this place,
so I thought I would come here

00:13:33.625 --> 00:13:35.875
and eat something, like I usually do...

00:13:35.875 --> 00:13:37.500
Hurry up and pick something!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:40.875
Oh, right! I'm sorry! Um, what was it again...?

00:13:40.875 --> 00:13:43.083
I'd already chosen something...

00:13:56.333 --> 00:13:58.167
You're going again today?

00:13:58.167 --> 00:13:59.542
Yes.

00:13:59.542 --> 00:14:01.792
But today is the day we had set aside

00:14:01.792 --> 00:14:04.292
to go eat those
strawberry tarts in the cafeteria.

00:14:04.292 --> 00:14:06.042
Why are you so determined?

00:14:06.042 --> 00:14:09.167
Because I'm a weapon, too.

00:14:09.167 --> 00:14:13.958
I was always pampered growing up.
If I'd been abandoned in Brooklyn,

00:14:13.958 --> 00:14:18.417
maybe I <i>would </i>have been dead in three days.

00:14:18.417 --> 00:14:22.000
There's nothing wrong with ordering
what I want in a cafe, is there?!

00:14:28.125 --> 00:14:29.583
"Pilaf"

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:34.333
What is it with this shop? It's the worst!

00:14:34.333 --> 00:14:36.500
They've got a lousy attitude, huh?

00:14:37.542 --> 00:14:39.000
All right!

00:14:40.208 --> 00:14:42.417
Hello.

00:14:56.542 --> 00:14:58.125
You again.

00:14:58.125 --> 00:15:01.875
U-Uh... m-may I order?

00:15:04.125 --> 00:15:05.250
U-Um...

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.667
Hunh?

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:16.042
One pilaf, please... One pilaf, please...

00:15:16.042 --> 00:15:17.875
Tsugumi?

00:15:17.875 --> 00:15:19.083
Yo!

00:15:19.083 --> 00:15:20.125
Heading out?

00:15:20.125 --> 00:15:22.667
Yes! To Deathbucks Caffe!

00:15:22.667 --> 00:15:24.708
You sure seem fired up, huh?

00:15:24.708 --> 00:15:28.875
Yeah. Right now, for me,
that's where the street is!

00:15:28.875 --> 00:15:30.708
Huh?

00:15:30.708 --> 00:15:32.583
This is a real fight!

00:15:46.417 --> 00:15:48.083
Hello.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:56.375
Um, one pilaf, please!

00:15:56.375 --> 00:15:58.375
I didn't ask you for your order.

00:15:58.375 --> 00:15:59.708
Huh?!

00:15:59.708 --> 00:16:02.333
Why do you come here every day?

00:16:02.333 --> 00:16:06.292
Uh... Why do you think?

00:16:06.292 --> 00:16:08.208
Are you trying to start a fight?!

00:16:08.208 --> 00:16:11.583
No! I don't mean it like that!

00:16:11.583 --> 00:16:13.667
Hey! Be careful!

00:16:13.667 --> 00:16:14.417
Hunh?

00:16:14.417 --> 00:16:17.917
It got on my shoes, right?
Go get something to wipe it up, right now!

00:16:17.917 --> 00:16:21.500
<i>You </i>wipe it up. Your face is raggy enough.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:22.917
What did you say?!

00:16:22.917 --> 00:16:27.083
How dare you treat a
customer like this, you scum!

00:16:27.083 --> 00:16:28.750
Why, you...!

00:16:34.958 --> 00:16:36.542
No, don't!

00:16:46.917 --> 00:16:52.125
I'm okay! I'm okay!
I just slipped on some coffee.

00:17:01.875 --> 00:17:05.292
It startled me that
I was bleeding, so I screamed.

00:17:05.292 --> 00:17:07.667
And then, everyone totally panicked.

00:17:07.667 --> 00:17:08.792
And then?!

00:17:08.792 --> 00:17:13.208
Miss Anya, you don't have to
be so upset. It wasn't on purpose.

00:17:13.208 --> 00:17:15.208
Miss Tsugumi, you're taking this too easy!

00:17:15.208 --> 00:17:21.250
You have to raise a loud, clear protest
against such unreasonable violence!

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:23.708
Are you okay, Tsugumi?!

00:17:23.708 --> 00:17:25.625
Patty, grab a towel from the counter!

00:17:25.625 --> 00:17:26.500
Yeah.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.500
Liz, there's a first-aid kit
in the lockers in back.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.625
Y-Yeah...

00:17:31.625 --> 00:17:34.792
This wasn't my fault!
You did this all on your own!

00:17:34.792 --> 00:17:35.792
Why, you...!

00:17:35.792 --> 00:17:37.917
Sir!

00:17:37.917 --> 00:17:39.542
Please leave.

00:17:40.833 --> 00:17:42.250
I'm never coming back here!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.042
Liz!

00:17:43.042 --> 00:17:46.708
Where in the lockers in back?! Ow!

00:17:50.042 --> 00:17:52.333
Hold on, Miss Tsugumi...?

00:17:52.333 --> 00:17:55.208
She must have been hit harder than we thought.

00:17:58.375 --> 00:18:00.208
What the hell are you doing here?!

00:18:00.208 --> 00:18:02.500
Are you here spying on us again?!

00:18:03.583 --> 00:18:06.083
If you're not gonna order,
then get out, right now!

00:18:06.083 --> 00:18:07.792
You're bothering the other customers!

00:18:07.792 --> 00:18:11.208
There are no other customers, thanks to you.

00:18:11.208 --> 00:18:13.292
I told you to do a good job.

00:18:13.292 --> 00:18:15.167
What do you think community service is for?

00:18:15.167 --> 00:18:17.458
Shut up! Beat it!

00:18:25.417 --> 00:18:26.917
Pardon me.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.750
E-Eh?!

00:18:31.417 --> 00:18:33.250
Golden eyes...

00:18:35.917 --> 00:18:37.250
Excuse me...

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.750
Hmm... There.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:42.958
Now you're symmetrical.

00:18:42.958 --> 00:18:44.542
I beg your pardon.

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:48.583
Symmetrical?

00:18:53.625 --> 00:18:54.583
I'm bored.

00:18:54.583 --> 00:18:58.750
Tch! We're doing everything we're supposed to.

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:01.917
We're even wearing these frilly uniforms.

00:19:01.917 --> 00:19:03.708
We can't help it, can we?!

00:19:03.708 --> 00:19:06.958
Up to now, we've lived so as
not to take any crap from anyone!

00:19:06.958 --> 00:19:11.625
How are we supposed to suddenly act
pleasant and endear ourselves to others?!

00:19:11.625 --> 00:19:15.125
I know that you are trying hard.
No one's asking you to--

00:19:15.125 --> 00:19:18.083
That's just empty talk!

00:19:18.083 --> 00:19:22.083
There's nobody who really understands us.

00:19:25.458 --> 00:19:27.208
Please excuse me.

00:19:30.708 --> 00:19:33.542
Why do you always come here?

00:19:33.542 --> 00:19:35.833
You get caught up in fights with us,

00:19:35.833 --> 00:19:38.500
and get yourself slugged.
You playing us for chumps?

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:39.833
No, not at all.

00:19:39.833 --> 00:19:42.000
Are you saying you ain't afraid of us?

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:44.208
No, no, don't be ridiculous!

00:19:44.208 --> 00:19:47.292
I am afraid! I am afraid of you!

00:19:47.292 --> 00:19:52.833
I am afraid, but more than that,
I admire your strength.

00:19:52.833 --> 00:19:54.375
I hoped that by coming to the shop,

00:19:54.375 --> 00:19:58.542
I might become at least a
little bit stronger, like you two are.

00:19:58.542 --> 00:20:02.333
Also, Miss Liz and Miss Patty,
you may be scary at first glance,

00:20:02.333 --> 00:20:04.167
but you're also so cool...

00:20:04.167 --> 00:20:07.500
...and so pretty, too...

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:10.333
What are you talking about, you dope?

00:20:15.458 --> 00:20:17.083
What's wrong, Big Sister?

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:19.875
Is this the shop?

00:20:19.875 --> 00:20:21.000
Yeah.

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:25.417
The waitresses are way beautiful,
but have ridiculously bad attitudes.

00:20:25.417 --> 00:20:28.458
You do like getting told
off by pretty girls, huh?

00:20:28.458 --> 00:20:31.375
Now, they won't bring
you what you order, either.

00:20:31.375 --> 00:20:33.375
Well, that's no good.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:39.583
Ah! Miss Anya! Meme!

00:20:39.583 --> 00:20:41.833
We decided to come, too.

00:20:41.833 --> 00:20:43.875
All right! Come on in!

00:20:43.875 --> 00:20:47.167
Miss Anya was concerned about you, Tsugumi.

00:20:47.167 --> 00:20:50.708
I just wanted to have some tea.

00:20:50.708 --> 00:20:52.292
Ah, ma'am!

00:20:52.292 --> 00:20:55.000
Tsugumi, we're here to see your real fight.

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:57.042
The fight is over already.

00:20:57.042 --> 00:20:58.542
And I bet you lost, right?

00:20:58.542 --> 00:20:59.708
I did not!

00:20:59.708 --> 00:21:01.042
--You lost.
--Yes you did.

00:21:01.042 --> 00:21:03.333
--This place is not the same as the one you were in before.
--Miss Meme! Miss Anya, too!

00:21:03.333 --> 00:21:04.083
--This place is not the same as the one you were in before.
--At the worst, it was a tie!

00:21:04.083 --> 00:21:05.042
--There's no need to be defiant,
--At the worst, it was a tie!

00:21:05.042 --> 00:21:07.917
--or to ingratiate yourselves to everyone.
--Tsugumi, you're weak, so you shouldn't force things.

00:21:07.917 --> 00:21:10.000
--or to ingratiate yourselves to everyone.
--Not you too, Jackie, ma'am...

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:12.500
--Everyone sees each other's souls for who they are.
--You two are together a lot lately.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:13.333
--Everyone sees each other's souls for who they are.
--Huh?

00:21:13.333 --> 00:21:15.250
--That's the kind of town Death City is.
--You're buying today, Tsugumi.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.250
Huh?!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:20.583
I'm not agreeable to everyone, myself.

00:21:20.583 --> 00:21:22.542
Now, get to work.

00:21:26.917 --> 00:21:29.917
Grab a seat. We'll take your order.

00:21:30.917 --> 00:21:33.875
Don't you mean you'll "decide" our order?

00:21:36.333 --> 00:21:37.792
You may be right.

00:21:37.792 --> 00:21:40.292
Okay! One pilaf, please!

00:21:41.583 --> 00:21:43.500
Gagantous!

00:21:50.792 --> 00:21:52.625
Sorry to bother you on your day off.

00:21:52.625 --> 00:21:55.958
Not at all. He is the
Traitor we beat, after all.

00:21:55.958 --> 00:21:59.875
It's not like you had any
other plans on your day off, Clay.

00:21:59.875 --> 00:22:02.042
Oh, like <i>you </i>did?

00:22:02.042 --> 00:22:06.833
The suspect will be transferred
from here straight to below DWMA.

00:22:06.833 --> 00:22:11.167
You two will go with the police
to transfer the suspect to DWMA...

00:22:20.542 --> 00:22:21.875
You two, take the culprit!

00:22:21.875 --> 00:22:23.042
Right!

00:22:23.042 --> 00:22:24.208
What happened?!

00:22:24.208 --> 00:22:28.458
One of the staff just suddenly
went wild, and got to the suspect...

00:22:39.792 --> 00:22:45.292
While you are sleeping, we keep moving.

00:22:47.542 --> 00:22:51.708
<i>With a big wave and a "See you,"</i>

00:22:51.708 --> 00:22:58.625
<i>let's meet in the new day</i>

00:23:15.375 --> 00:23:19.542
<i>Our shadows stretch along the pavement</i>

00:23:19.542 --> 00:23:23.542
<i>coming together, then apart, then together</i>

00:23:23.542 --> 00:23:31.875
<i>What do I say when the road home ends?</i>

00:23:31.875 --> 00:23:36.042
<i>You are not alone. Nope, right nearby,</i>

00:23:36.042 --> 00:23:40.167
<i>there are eyes looking back at you</i>

00:23:40.167 --> 00:23:44.292
<i>And just like a miracle,</i>

00:23:44.292 --> 00:23:48.042
<i>they can turn even failures into laughter</i>

00:23:48.042 --> 00:23:52.167
<i>Thank you for a fun day</i>

00:23:52.167 --> 00:23:56.500
<i>Let's do it again tomorrow</i>

00:23:56.500 --> 00:24:00.583
<i>We'll open a brand-new door</i>

00:24:00.583 --> 00:24:04.750
<i>chasing after dreams and love</i>

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:10.375
<i>and those nameless feelings, too</i>

00:24:17.708 --> 00:24:20.458
Death Bazaar--that's the dream
festival where all the commoners

00:24:20.458 --> 00:24:23.375
gather and sell off the
things they no longer want.

00:24:23.375 --> 00:24:25.167
A bear eating a salmon? How neat!

00:24:25.167 --> 00:24:27.458
The salmon shouted! Get it?
[<i>sake</i>: salmon] [<i>sakenda</i>: shouted]

00:24:27.458 --> 00:24:28.625
The bear is in trouble!
[<i>kuma</i>: bear] [<i>kumatta</i>: (sic) in trouble]

00:24:28.625 --> 00:24:29.583
"Next time: Nice Day for a Death Bazaar!"
Get it?

00:24:29.583 --> 00:24:32.192
"Next time: Nice Day for a Death Bazaar!"
Is this a garbage dump?
